\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{The complex unit in a Pauli product}
\date{2026-11-13}

\p{The product of two Pauli operators in the declared matrix
representation satisfies #{\sigma_1\sigma_2=\ui\sigma_3}.
Mathematical physics writes #{i} in that product. Geometric
calculus writes the same relation with a unit bivector or the
pseudoscalar. The factor here is #{\ui}. A complex scalar
appears because the product is computed in that representation.}
